---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout current="resources" title="Useful resources">
  <section class="section page-section">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Appendix 08</p>
      <h1>Useful resources</h1>
      <p>
        A curated, opinionated list of papers, documentation, and courses to go
        deeper into agent engineering. Organized as a practical learning path for
        technical readers to move from core patterns to production systems.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="section-head compact-head" style="margin-top: 48px;">
      <p class="eyebrow">Recommended path</p>
      <h2>Follow this order for a technical deep dive.</h2>
    </div>

    <ul class="timeline-list">
      <li>
        <span class="timeline-number">01</span>
        <div>
          <strong>Agent fundamentals</strong>
          <p>Control loops, tool use, orchestration patterns, and what “effective” agent behavior looks like.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="timeline-number">02</span>
        <div>
          <strong>Runtime and context</strong>
          <p>Frameworks and protocols (ADK, MCP, skills, context engineering) that make systems composable and maintainable.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="timeline-number">03</span>
        <div>
          <strong>Reliability</strong>
          <p>Evals, benchmarking, reflection loops, and observability — the layer that makes agents production-safe.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="timeline-number">04</span>
        <div>
          <strong>Advanced practice</strong>
          <p>Multi-agent state transfer, CodeAct, and hands-on agent courses for end-to-end implementation.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <div class="section-head compact-head" style="margin-top: 48px;">
      <p class="eyebrow">Stage 01</p>
      <h2>Agent fundamentals.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="refs-grid">
      <a class="refs-block" href="https://www.anthropic.com/research/building-effective-agents" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        <span>Must read</span>
        <h3>Building Effective Agents</h3>
        <p>
          A clear thesis on why simple, composable patterns often outperform
          heavyweight autonomous designs in real-world systems.
        </p>
        <div class="refs-link">anthropic.com <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </a>

      <a class="refs-block" href="https://huggingface.co/agents-course" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        <span>Hugging Face</span>
        <h3>Agents Course</h3>
        <p>
          Practical track focused on planning, tool use, and implementation
          details for modern agentic systems.
        </p>
        <div class="refs-link">huggingface.co/agents-course <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </a>

      <a class="refs-block" href="https://www.philschmid.de/langgraph-gemini-2-5-react-agent" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        <span>Phil Schmid</span>
        <h3>ReAct Agent from Scratch (Gemini + LangGraph)</h3>
        <p>
          A modern implementation-level walk-through of the canonical ReAct loop
          with current model/runtime tooling.
        </p>
        <div class="refs-link">philschmid.de <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </a>

      <a class="refs-block" href="https://cloud.google.com/use-cases/ai-agents" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        <span>Architecture</span>
        <h3>Google Cloud Agents</h3>
        <p>
          High-level enterprise framing for deployment, grounding, and governance
          around agent applications.
        </p>
        <div class="refs-link">cloud.google.com <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="section-head compact-head" style="margin-top: 48px;">
      <p class="eyebrow">Stage 02</p>
      <h2>Runtime, protocol, and context engineering.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="refs-grid">
      <a class="refs-block" href="https://adk.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        <span>Framework</span>
        <h3>Google ADK</h3>
        <p>
          Runtime primitives for event loops, state, tool calling, and evaluation
          harnesses used across this deck.
        </p>
        <div class="refs-link">adk.dev <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </a>

      <a class="refs-block" href="https://modelcontextprotocol.io/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        <span>Protocol</span>
        <h3>Model Context Protocol (MCP)</h3>
        <p>
          Open interface layer for connecting models to external tools, resources,
          and data providers.
        </p>
        <div class="refs-link">modelcontextprotocol.io <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </a>

      <a class="refs-block" href="https://agentskills.io/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        <span>Standard</span>
        <h3>Agent Skills</h3>
        <p>
          Lightweight specification for packaging repeatable workflows into
          portable, version-controlled skill bundles.
        </p>
        <div class="refs-link">agentskills.io <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </a>

      <a class="refs-block" href="https://huggingface.co/learn/context-course" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        <span>Hugging Face</span>
        <h3>Context Course</h3>
        <p>
          Focused material for retrieval inputs, prompt structure, and preparing
          high-signal model context.
        </p>
        <div class="refs-link">huggingface.co/learn/context-course <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </a>

      <a class="refs-block" href="https://blog.langchain.dev/context-engineering/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        <span>LangChain</span>
        <h3>Context Engineering</h3>
        <p>
          Useful perspective on controlling context windows, tool exposure, and
          retrieval payloads as agent systems scale.
        </p>
        <div class="refs-link">blog.langchain.dev <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </a>

      <a class="refs-block" href="https://www.langchain.com/blog/context-management-for-deepagents" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        <span>LangChain</span>
        <h3>Context Management for Deep Agents</h3>
        <p>
          Practical patterns for long-running agent workflows where summaries,
          task state, and retrieval context can drift over time.
        </p>
        <div class="refs-link">langchain.com/blog <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </a>

      <a class="refs-block" href="https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langchain/context-engineering" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        <span>LangChain Docs</span>
        <h3>Context engineering docs</h3>
        <p>
          Implementation guidance for structuring context, reducing confusion,
          and preventing low-signal context from degrading agent behavior.
        </p>
        <div class="refs-link">docs.langchain.com <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </a>

      <a class="refs-block" href="https://www.philschmid.de/mcp-introduction" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        <span>Phil Schmid</span>
        <h3>MCP Overview</h3>
        <p>
          Implementation-oriented introduction to MCP as the boundary between
          agent runtimes and external capabilities.
        </p>
        <div class="refs-link">philschmid.de <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </a>

      <a class="refs-block" href="https://www.philschmid.de/memory-in-agents" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        <span>Phil Schmid</span>
        <h3>Memory in Agents</h3>
        <p>
          Practical architecture patterns for persistent memory and recall.
        </p>
        <div class="refs-link">philschmid.de <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </a>

      <a class="refs-block" href="https://huggingface.co/learn/agents-course/unit2/smolagents/introduction" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        <span>Hugging Face</span>
        <h3>smolagents introduction</h3>
        <p>
          A code-first mini track for lightweight agent implementations and rapid
          experimentation.
        </p>
        <div class="refs-link">huggingface.co/learn/agents-course <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="section-head compact-head" style="margin-top: 48px;">
      <p class="eyebrow">Memory systems</p>
      <h2>Curated memory architecture, implementation, and safety references.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="refs-grid">
      <a class="refs-block" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.03442" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        <span>Concepts</span>
        <h3>Generative Agents</h3>
        <p>
          Canonical memory architecture reference introducing memory streams,
          reflection, and planning loops for agent behavior.
        </p>
        <div class="refs-link">arxiv.org/abs/2304.03442 <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </a>

      <a class="refs-block" href="https://github.com/mem0ai/mem0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        <span>Framework</span>
        <h3>Mem0</h3>
        <p>
          Open-source memory layer for adding persistent, evolving memory to
          assistants and agent systems.
        </p>
        <div class="refs-link">github.com/mem0ai/mem0 <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </a>

      <a class="refs-block" href="https://blog.langchain.dev/langmem/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        <span>Framework</span>
        <h3>LangMem SDK (LangChain)</h3>
        <p>
          Official long-term memory SDK patterns for episodic and semantic memory
          inside LangGraph-style agent loops.
        </p>
        <div class="refs-link">blog.langchain.dev/langmem <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </a>

      <a class="refs-block" href="https://www.digitalocean.com/community/tutorials/langgraph-mem0-integration-long-term-ai-memory" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        <span>Implementation</span>
        <h3>Long-term memory with Mem0 + LangGraph</h3>
        <p>
          Practical wiring guide for integrating persistent memory into cyclical
          agent workflows.
        </p>
        <div class="refs-link">digitalocean.com/community/tutorials <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </a>

      <a class="refs-block" href="https://github.com/sambanova/toolbench" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        <span>Benchmark</span>
        <h3>ToolBench</h3>
        <p>
          Large-scale benchmark for tool-use sequencing and multi-step execution,
          useful for memory-sensitive trajectory evaluation.
        </p>
        <div class="refs-link">github.com/sambanova/toolbench <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </a>

      <a class="refs-block" href="https://huggingface.co/spaces/gaia-benchmark/leaderboard" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        <span>Benchmark</span>
        <h3>GAIA benchmark</h3>
        <p>
          Real-world assistant benchmark where multi-step reasoning and memory
          retention materially affect task completion quality.
        </p>
        <div class="refs-link">huggingface.co/spaces/gaia-benchmark <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </a>

      <a class="refs-block" href="https://aclanthology.org/2025.acl-long.1227.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        <span>Privacy</span>
        <h3>Unveiling Privacy Risks in LLM Agent Memory</h3>
        <p>
          ACL paper on leakage and misuse risks in persistent memory stores for
          agentic systems.
        </p>
        <div class="refs-link">aclanthology.org/2025.acl-long.1227 <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </a>

      <a class="refs-block" href="https://arxiv.org/html/2603.11768v1" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        <span>Governance</span>
        <h3>Governing Evolving Memory in LLM Agents</h3>
        <p>
          Taxonomy of memory-corruption failure modes and governance patterns for
          safe long-lived memory systems.
        </p>
        <div class="refs-link">arxiv.org/html/2603.11768v1 <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="section-head compact-head" style="margin-top: 48px;">
      <p class="eyebrow">RAG systems</p>
      <h2>Curated resources for retrieval-augmented generation.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="refs-grid">
      <a class="refs-block" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.11401" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        <span>Fundamentals</span>
        <h3>Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) paper</h3>
        <p>
          The canonical paper that defined the modern retrieval + generation
          architecture for knowledge-intensive tasks.
        </p>
        <div class="refs-link">arxiv.org/abs/2005.11401 <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </a>

      <a class="refs-block" href="https://www.llamaindex.ai/blog/evaluating-the-ideal-chunk-size-for-a-rag-system-using-llamaindex-6207e54443f0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        <span>Fundamentals</span>
        <h3>Chunking strategy and retrieval quality</h3>
        <p>
          Practical analysis of how chunk size and overlap affect recall and
          precision in real RAG pipelines.
        </p>
        <div class="refs-link">llamaindex.ai/blog <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </a>

      <a class="refs-block" href="https://unstructured.io/blog/improving-retrieval-in-rag-with-reranking" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        <span>Fundamentals</span>
        <h3>Reranking for better top-k precision</h3>
        <p>
          Hands-on guide to reranking as one of the highest-leverage retrieval
          quality improvements in production.
        </p>
        <div class="refs-link">unstructured.io/blog <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </a>

      <a class="refs-block" href="https://www.llamaindex.ai/blog/rag-is-dead-long-live-agentic-retrieval" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        <span>Agentic RAG</span>
        <h3>From static RAG to agentic retrieval</h3>
        <p>
          Why single-shot retrieval is often insufficient and how agents can
          route, iterate, and refine retrieval over multiple steps.
        </p>
        <div class="refs-link">llamaindex.ai/blog <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </a>

      <a class="refs-block" href="https://github.com/asinghcsu/AgenticRAG-Survey" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        <span>Agentic RAG</span>
        <h3>Agentic RAG survey</h3>
        <p>
          Curated survey repository covering multi-hop, corrective, and planning-
          driven retrieval approaches.
        </p>
        <div class="refs-link">github.com/asinghcsu/AgenticRAG-Survey <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </a>

      <a class="refs-block" href="https://docs.ragas.io/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        <span>Evaluation</span>
        <h3>Ragas documentation</h3>
        <p>
          Widely used framework for evaluating RAG pipelines with metrics for
          answer quality, faithfulness, and context use.
        </p>
        <div class="refs-link">docs.ragas.io <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </a>

      <a class="refs-block" href="https://www.trulens.org/trulens_eval/core_concepts_rag_triad/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        <span>Evaluation</span>
        <h3>TruLens RAG triad</h3>
        <p>
          Clear evaluation framework built around context relevance,
          groundedness, and answer relevance.
        </p>
        <div class="refs-link">trulens.org <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </a>

      <a class="refs-block" href="https://arize.com/docs/phoenix/cookbook/evaluation/evaluate-rag" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        <span>Evaluation</span>
        <h3>Evaluate RAG with Arize Phoenix</h3>
        <p>
          Practical cookbook for tracing and scoring retrieval quality and
          groundedness with observability in the loop.
        </p>
        <div class="refs-link">arize.com/docs/phoenix <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </a>

      <a class="refs-block" href="https://www.redhat.com/en/blog/planning-design-your-production-grade-rag-system" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        <span>Operations</span>
        <h3>Planning a production-grade RAG system</h3>
        <p>
          Covers freshness strategy, re-indexing, access controls, and operational
          design concerns for enterprise deployment.
        </p>
        <div class="refs-link">redhat.com/en/blog <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </a>

      <a class="refs-block" href="https://dev.to/gursharansingh/rag-in-production-what-breaks-after-launch-5912" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        <span>Operations</span>
        <h3>RAG in production: what breaks after launch</h3>
        <p>
          High-signal operational checklist on drift, caching, invalidation, and
          failure patterns seen in live systems.
        </p>
        <div class="refs-link">dev.to <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="section-head compact-head" style="margin-top: 48px;">
      <p class="eyebrow">Stage 03</p>
      <h2>Reliability: evals, reflection, and observability.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="refs-grid">
      <a class="refs-block" href="https://blog.langchain.dev/benchmarking-agent-tool-use/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        <span>LangChain</span>
        <h3>Benchmarking Agent Tool Use</h3>
        <p>
          Practical methodology for measuring whether agents pick correct tools
          and trajectories, not just plausible final text.
        </p>
        <div class="refs-link">blog.langchain.dev <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </a>

      <a class="refs-block" href="https://blog.langchain.dev/reflection-agents/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        <span>LangChain</span>
        <h3>Reflection Agents</h3>
        <p>
          Concrete generate-critique-revise loops to improve output quality under
          explicit rubrics.
        </p>
        <div class="refs-link">blog.langchain.dev <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </a>

      <a class="refs-block" href="https://www.philschmid.de/testing-skills" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        <span>Phil Schmid</span>
        <h3>Evaluating and Testing Agent Skills</h3>
        <p>
          A practical bridge from informal “vibe checks” to reproducible
