        </p>
        <div class="refs-link">langfuse.com <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </a>

      <a class="refs-block" href="https://www.comet.com/docs/opik" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        <span>Platform</span>
        <h3>Opik</h3>
        <p>
          End-to-end open-source platform for evaluating, testing, and tracking
          LLM and agent applications.
        </p>
        <div class="refs-link">comet.com/docs/opik <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </a>

      <a class="refs-block" href="https://arize.com/phoenix/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        <span>Platform</span>
        <h3>Arize Phoenix</h3>
        <p>
          Observability + evaluation suite for trajectory inspection and
          LLM-as-a-judge workflows.
        </p>
        <div class="refs-link">arize.com/phoenix <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="section-head compact-head" style="margin-top: 48px;">
      <p class="eyebrow">Stage 04</p>
      <h2>Advanced implementation and scaling patterns.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="refs-grid">
      <a class="refs-block" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2402.01030" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        <span>Research</span>
        <h3>CodeAct Paper</h3>
        <p>
          "Executable Code is a General Action Space for Large Language Models."
          A key reference for why code execution can outperform JSON actions.
        </p>
        <div class="refs-link">arxiv.org <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </a>

      <a class="refs-block" href="https://blog.langchain.dev/command-a-new-tool-for-multi-agent-architectures-in-langgraph/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        <span>LangChain</span>
        <h3>Multi-agent communication with Command</h3>
        <p>
          Updated state-transfer patterns for specialist-agent coordination and
          graph-based orchestration.
        </p>
        <div class="refs-link">blog.langchain.dev <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </a>

      <a class="refs-block" href="https://www.kaggle.com/learn/ai-agents" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        <span>Kaggle</span>
        <h3>AI Agents Intensive</h3>
        <p>
          Hands-on practical track for building and evaluating agent workflows.
        </p>
        <div class="refs-link">kaggle.com/learn/ai-agents <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </a>
    </div>

    <p class="mechanism-note">
      This page is intentionally living documentation. We can keep expanding it
      as better benchmarks, courses, and production playbooks emerge.
    </p>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
